{"name":"Sandy Cove","hex":"#ceb587","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Sandy Cove","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A town in Newfoundland, Newfoundland and Labrador, Canada."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Sandy_Cove"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sandy Cove, Newfoundland and Labrador","blocks":[{"text":"Sandy Cove is a town located on the Eastport Peninsula in Newfoundland and Labrador, Canada. It is located on Newman Sound, which is part of Bonavista Bay. It had a population of 120 in the 2021 census."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/NLC_Eastport1_tango7174.jpg/330px-NLC_Eastport1_tango7174.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sandy_Cove%2C_Newfoundland_and_Labrador","wikidata":"Q7417210"},{"title":"Cove","blocks":[{"text":"A cove is a small bay or coastal inlet. They usually have narrow, restricted entrances, are often circular or oval, and are often situated within a larger bay. Small, narrow, sheltered bays, inlets, tidal creeks, or recesses in a coast are often considered coves."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/McWay_cove_1.jpg/330px-McWay_cove_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cove","wikidata":"Q31615"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/NLC_Eastport2_tango7174.jpg/500px-NLC_Eastport2_tango7174.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/NLC_Eastport2_tango7174.jpg/1280px-NLC_Eastport2_tango7174.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/NLC_Eastport2_tango7174.jpg/500px-NLC_Eastport2_tango7174.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANLC_Eastport2_tango7174.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/NLC_Eastport1_tango7174.jpg/500px-NLC_Eastport1_tango7174.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/NLC_Eastport1_tango7174.jpg/500px-NLC_Eastport1_tango7174.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sandy Cove Beach","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANLC_Eastport1_tango7174.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/McWay_cove_1.jpg/500px-McWay_cove_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/McWay_cove_1.jpg/1280px-McWay_cove_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/McWay_cove_1.jpg/500px-McWay_cove_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"McWay Cove, California, United States","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMcWay_cove_1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a8/Figure_lulworth_formation.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a8/Figure_lulworth_formation.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Map showing two examples of how coves form. The rock types are those of Lulworth Cove. In example A, a river breaks through the resistant chalk back rock and limestone, leaving the weak clays to be rapidly eroded. In example B, the sea breaks through the limestone, perhaps by forming a cave, and then erodes the clay away.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFigure_lulworth_formation.png"}],"sounds":{}}}